['{
  "question": "What is the current in a circuit with a 12 V battery and a 4 \u03a9 resistor?",
  "answer": "Using Ohm's Law (V = I \u00d7 R), the current (I) can be calculated as I = V / R = 12 V / 4 \u03a9 = 3 A. Therefore, the current in the circuit is 3 amperes.",
