  "answer": "Water is a liquid, and ice is a solid. Water takes the shape of its container and does not have a fixed volume, while ice has a fixed shape and volume. This comparison tells us that ice is a solid because it maintains its shape and volume, whereas water, as a liquid, changes shape to fit its container. Therefore, the state of matter depends on how the substance behaves in terms of shape and volume.",
