['{
  "question": "At chemical equilibrium, what happens to the concentrations of reactants and products?",
  "answer": "At chemical equilibrium, the concentrations of reactants and products remain constant because the forward and reverse reactions occur at the same rate. This means that reactants are converted to products at the same rate as products are converted back to reactants, resulting in no net change in concentrations.",
